    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="9">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Episc">Episc</ref> 9</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9" corresp="#wit-x"><pb n="478" ed="#liebermann"/>Eallum Cristenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mannu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gebyreð, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi riht lufian ⁊ unriht ascunian; ⁊ huru gehadode men scylon á riht reran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ unriht alecgan; þy sculon bisceopas mid worulddeman domas dihtan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi ne geþafian, gyf his waldan magan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ðær ænig unriht up aspringe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="9" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.10"/><pb n="478" ed="#liebermann"/>Christianis (autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.9"/>) omnibus opus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.4"/> (necessarium) est, ut rectum diligant et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.11"/> iniqua condempnent; et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.12"/> saltem sacris ordinibus euecti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.13"/> rectum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.4"/> (iustum) semper erigant et iniustum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.4"/> (praua) deponant. Ideo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.4"/> (Hinc) debent episcopi cum seculi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.14"/> iudicibus iudicia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.15"/> dictare (interesse iudiciis), ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.16"/> permittant, si possint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.17"/>, ut aliquid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.4"/> iniustum illuc pullulet (illinc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Episc_9.lnote.oe.18"/> aliqua prauitatum germina pullulauerint).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-x"><pb n="104" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Eallum Cristenum mannum gebyreð þæt hi riht lufian and unriht ascunian; and huru gehadode men scylon a riht reran and unriht alecgan; þy sculon bisceopas mid worulddeman domas dihtan, þæt hi ne geþafian, gyf his waldan magan, þæt ðær ænig unriht up aspringe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="478" ed="#liebermann"/>Allen Christenmenschen gebührt, dass sie Recht lieben und Unrecht verabscheuen; und vollends geweihte Männer [Kleriker] sollen immer Recht erhöhen und Unrecht unterdrücken; darum sollen Bischöfe mit weltlichen Richtern die Rechtsurtheile<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Episc_9.lnote.de.1"/> bestimmen, so dass sie nicht erlauben, wenn sie darob verfügen können, dass da irgend ein Unrecht entspringe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It befits all Christian people to love right and abhor wrong; and above all ordained men [clerics] must always raise up right and suppress wrong; therefore bishops must direct judgments together with secular judges, so that they do not allow, if they have power over it, any wrong to spring up there.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-x"><pb n="105" ed="#rabin-doml"/>It is proper for all Christians to love righteousness and hate injustice; and indeed, men in orders must always support what is right and reject what is wrong; thus, bishops must pronounce sentences with secular judges so that they do not permit, if it is in their power, any injustice to spring up there.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="478"><ref target="clause:Episc_4">Episc 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">s. o. 4</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Episc_4">Episc 4</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Line breaks and spacing inside K were tidied. Liebermann compares 4.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">bishops must pronounce: This clause marks one of the most significant points of conflict between Wulfstan and Ælfric, who strongly opposed cooperation between ecclesiastics and secular judges.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXIIII Quintum qui pertinet omnibus Christianis <hi rend="italic">überschreibt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">K has the heading XXIIII Quintum qui pertinet omnibus Christianis</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Lond.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond; eingeklammertes übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the text before the bracket Lond; the bracketed text the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et — euecti <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et — euecti omitted in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. et <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. et Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">euicti <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">euicti R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> iu. di. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> in. iudiciis, iudicia di. [<hi rend="italic">d. h. Glosse vor ursprünglicher Lesung</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Or; nur</hi> in. iu. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only iu. di. K; in. iudiciis, iudicia di. [i.e. a gloss placed before the original reading] Or; only in. iu. the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nec <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nec Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-sunt <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-sunt Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illum <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">illum R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">478</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ræran <hi rend="italic">Tho.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ræran Tho.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Episc_9.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">271</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 4¹. 8¹. Offenbar ist hier Schiedsgericht nicht allein gemeint, sondern u. a. die Teilnahme am Grafschaftsgericht (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 6 ff.) neben dem Ealdorman</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 4¹. 8¹. Evidently arbitration alone is not meant here, but, among other things, participation in the shire court (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 6 ff.) alongside the ealdorman</seg></note>
      </div>
